<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hartenstein, Saxony</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hartenstein is a small town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwickauer-mulde">Zwickauer Mulde</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, at the edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ore-mountains">Ore Mountains</a>. Its lordship, with Hartenstein Castle and the nearby Burg Stein, was bought by the Schönburg family in 1406 and held by them under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> overlordship. It is the birthplace of the poet Paul Fleming.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hartenstein-saxony.jpg" alt="Hartenstein, Saxony" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kora27 · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hartenstein._Sachsen._Erzgebirge.IMG_2301WI.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
